{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"26c883e7-64a0-4d60-9871-d3ed09b5cc38","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\n  \"doc_id\": \"keepass\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-001\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"must be downloaded and installed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without specifying who performs the download and installation, or from where and onto which target environment KeePass is installed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-002\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Master Password has no limits in length. A whole sentence can be used with more than 100 characters.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits minimum length constraints (such as whether an empty password is permitted) and allowed character set/encoding, and leaves unclear whether \u003e100 characters is a required support threshold or merely an example.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The demonstrative 'that' has multiple plausible antecedents ('Folder selected', 'type', or 'the database'), and referring to a '.kdb' file as a 'Folder' creates ambiguity over whether a directory or a file is expected.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies a file/type validation on selection without defining what happens if an incompatible or unreadable item is selected, and omits the selecting actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The phrase 'if selected' has an unclear referent (new vs. existing database), 'the previews one' is ambiguous when multiple databases exist, and 'different names' omits scope (same folder vs. globally).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without naming which actor or system component performs the selection and replacement, and omits whether user confirmation or warning is required before overwriting.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-005\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There must be entries in the database in order for them to be printed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a precondition for printing without defining system behavior when the database contains no entries (e.g., disabled print option vs. error message), and omits the printing actor via passive voice ('to be printed').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'All data related to' is unquantified and leaves unclear which entry fields are searched, whether matching is case-sensitive or partial, and whether full entries or only matching fields are displayed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes a lookup operation on the happy path without specifying behavior when no entries match or the query is empty; also omits search scope and uses passive voice ('must be shown') without naming the display component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-007\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the new group/subgroup to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a required-name validation for creating a group/subgroup without specifying what happens if the name is empty, invalid, or duplicate, and omits the actor via passive voice ('to be created').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-008\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A subgroup cannot be created when no group is selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a precondition blocking subgroup creation without specifying how the system prevents or responds to an attempt (e.g., disabled action vs. error prompt), and omits actors via passive voice ('cannot be created', 'is selected').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-009\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the group/subgroup to be renamed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a required-name validation for renaming without specifying what happens when the name is missing, invalid, or duplicate, and omits the actor via passive voice ('to be renamed').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"find something in a group a word\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'something' and 'a word' are vague, leaving unclear which entry attributes or subgroups are searched and whether phrases, substrings, or case-insensitive matching are supported.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without identifying who enters the search term or which component performs the search, and omits error/no-match handling when the find field is empty or yields no results.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The trailing infinitive 'to be created' can syntactically attach either to 'group' (requiring a group to be created) or to 'entry' (requiring an existing group in order to create an entry).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a creation precondition without specifying system behavior if entry creation is attempted when no group is selected or exists, and omits the actor via passive voice ('to be created').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-012\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is completed the repeat password field must be completed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a form validation rule without specifying what happens if the repeat password field is left incomplete; also uses passive voice without naming the actor and omits which screen or operation this applies to.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Password field and repeat password field must be identical\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States an equality validation constraint without specifying what happens when the two fields do not match or when and where the check is triggered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must be selected to be viewed or modified\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a precondition for viewing or modifying an entry without specifying system behavior when no entry is selected (e.g., disabled controls vs. error prompt), and omits the actor via passive voice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is changed the repeat password field must be Changed and be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a validation rule on password modification without specifying what happens if the repeat password field is not changed or does not match, and omits the actor via passive voice ('is changed', 'must be Changed').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"evidence\": \"be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-013\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Repeats the requirement that the password field and repeat password field must be identical, which is already stated unconditionally in KP-013.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-016\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must be selected before it is duplicated\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a precondition for duplicating an entry without specifying system behavior when no entry is selected, and omits the actor via passive voice ('must be selected', 'is duplicated').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-017\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"download new language translations For the following features, use cases are not included\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Missing punctuation merges two separate clauses, and the demonstrative reference 'the following features' is ambiguous as to which subsequent requirements lack use cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-017\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An internet connection and a browser are required in order to download new language translations\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies external dependencies (internet connection and browser) without defining behavior when offline, when no browser is available, or when download fails; also omits the initiating actor and how translations are applied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-018\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The prefix “Auto-Type:” is required in front of each sequence\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits where sequences are placed (e.g., in an entry's note field) and when they are evaluated, as well as error or fallback behavior if the 'Auto-Type:' prefix is missing or malformed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-019\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Sequence’s length\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Sequence’s length' is ambiguous as to whether the 59-character limit includes the required 'Auto-Type:' prefix (KP-018) or counts only the keystroke