sed (e.g., error exit, warning, or opening only the first).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-021\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"database file\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Refers to the '.kdb' target as a 'database file', whereas KP-003 refers to it as 'Folder' ('Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-022\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In case a space is found in the path, it must be enclosed into quotes\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The pronoun 'it' has two plausible antecedents—'a space' (nearest singular noun) and 'the path' (intended referent)—and 'quotes' does not specify single vs. double quotes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"is found in the path, it must be enclosed into quotes\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without naming who encloses the path or which component parses it, omits that this applies to command-line options, and specifies no error handling for unquoted paths containing spaces.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-023\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the database doesn’t open unless the password is entered\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes a master password authentication check without specifying what happens when the entered password is incorrect or omitted (e.g., error message, retry behavior, or delay/lockout).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the database doesn’t open unless the key file is present\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes a key-file authentication check without specifying what happens if the key file is missing, unreadable, or invalid, and leaves 'present' (required path or location) undefined.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-025\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If there is a composite key, both master password and key file are required\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a composite-key authentication requirement without specifying system behavior or error handling when either credential is missing or invalid.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats are not specialized password database formats\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'File formats' does not specify which formats are covered, and 'specialized password database formats' is subjective and undefined with no testable criterion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-028\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats are not specialized password database formats\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits the scope and context—specifically which file formats (native '.kdb' storage vs. import/export formats) this constraint applies to.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats only specify a low-level layout of stored data\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'File formats' leaves unspecified which formats are meant, 'low-level layout' is unquantified and undefined, and the scope of 'only' is syntactically unclear.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-029\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats only specify a low-level layout of stored data\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits which file formats are being specified and does not define what the low-level layout includes or excludes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-030\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Global hot key cannot be changed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"References 'Global hot key' without specifying what the fixed key combination is, what action it triggers, or how attempts to change it or OS shortcut conflicts are handled.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","duration_seconds":140.373412,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":14885,"output_tokens":29019,"thinking_tokens":24334,"cache_read_tokens":12831,"total_tokens":43904}}}
